Description:
Put a chest next to any number of machines (like furnaces or crystalariums), and they'll take raw items from the chest and push their finished items into it. Press [font=Courier New]U[/font] (configurable) to show an automation overlay:
<br />[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Pathoschild/StardewMods/stable/Automate/docs/screenshots/iridium-mead-factory.png[/img]
<br />
<br />[b][color=#6aa84f][b][color=#6aa84f][b][color=#6aa84f]For non-English players, translations are included in the base mod. [url=https://github.com/Pathoschild/StardewMods#translating-the-mods]Contributions are welcome[/url]![/color][/b][/color][/b][/color][/b]
<br />
<br />
<br />[size=6][b]Install[/b][/size][list=1]
<br />[*][url=https://smapi.io]Install the latest version of SMAPI[/url].
<br />[*]Unzip the mod folder into [font=Courier New]Stardew Valley/Mods[/font].
<br />[*]Run the game using SMAPI.
<br />[/list]
<br />[b]Careful:[/b] the shipping bin will sell items by default. Make sure to move chests away from the shipping bin if needed, or see [i]Settings[/i] below to turn it off.
<br />
<br />
<br />[size=6][b]Settings[/b][/size]
<br />Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/5098]Generic Mod Config Menu[/url] to change how Automate works ([url=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Pathoschild/StardewMods/stable/Automate/docs/screenshots/generic-config-menu.png]see screenshot[/url]).
<br />
<br />For example, you can...
<br />[list]
<br />[*]turn off the shipping bin, so it won't sell items automatically (under "Shipping Bin settings");
<br />[*]let paths connect machines together (under "Enabled connectors");
<br />[*]configure individual machine types;
<br />[*]and more.
<br />[/list]
<br />
<br />[size=6][b]How to use it[/b][/size]
<br />Place a chest next to a crafting machine (in any direction including diagonal) to connect it. Machines connected to a chest will push their output into it, and pull ingredients to process out of it.
<br />
<br />If you have multiple chests connected to a machine, all the input for a recipe needs to be in the same chest (e.g. a furnace won't work with coal in one chest and ores in the other).
<br />
